  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of integrated humanitarian lifesaving assistance and services to most vulnerable conflict-affected population, including children and women in Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), education, nutrition, child protection, and mine action assistance to vulnerable communities affected by conflict in Myanmar. This UNICEF project supports access to education for children, screens for and treats acute malnutrition, protects children through the establishment of child-friendly spaces, delivers explosive ordnance risk education, and provides access to clean water, sanitation and hygiene facilities, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 13,000 people in the Education sector, 24,315 people in the Nutrition sector, 5,750 people in the Protection &#x2013; Child Protection sector, 80,000 people in the Protection &#x2013; Mine Action sector, and 40,000 people in the WASH sector.</narrative>
  </description>
